WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.920
In 1980, Condea Vista announced that EDC [ethylene dichloride] had been leaked into the Mossville groundwater?

2
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.700
See I didn't . . .

3
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:12.420
Do you remember much about that?

4
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.660
No I don't.

5
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:23.620
The first I remember about the EDC situation was in the nineties when the class- action lawsuit came about.

6
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:27.360
I didn't know anything about it before then.

7
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.340
Were you surprised to hear that?

8
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.100
Yes I was.

9
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.740
Yeah because like I said my mother was still living in the community,

10
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:43.500
my in-laws were still there, and they didn't know anything about it either until this lawsuit came about.

11
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:50.340
And that's around the time when the buyout came about in the late nineties,

12
00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:54.620
like '98, because my mother lived there until that time, and so did my in-laws.

13
00:00:54.620 --> 00:01:01.720
And I guess a lot of things that went on a lot of people wouldn't talk to me about it because maybe they felt,

14
00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:11.620
because I worked for the industry, that I would be biased if they said something to me about it, or to my mother.

15
00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:16.960
So I think that's the reason I didn't hear a lot of what was going on.

16
00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.740
Do you know anything about the effort to clean up the area?

17
00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:19.940
Did you hear . . .?

18
00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.160
I remember, you know,

19
00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:31.520
that there was a big effort between the two companies Condea Vista . . . I think it was still Condea Vista at the time and maybe it was Sasol,

20
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:37.740
I can't really remember, and Conoco to get that cleaned up.

21
00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:48.020
In 1997, I believe that's when they were doing blood tests and finding that Mossville residents had a higher level of dioxin in their blood?

22
00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.840
I remember seeing that on the news and hearing about it, yes.

23
00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:51.500
Yeah.

24
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.720
What . . . Do you remember what people were talking about during that time?

25
00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:55.620
Were people worried?

26
00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:56.820
Were you worried?

27
00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.880
No, I wasn't worried.

28
00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.020
I remember people saying, you know,

29
00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:10.160
that a lot of that had come from the EDC leak and that's what had made the dioxins into their system.

30
00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:19.380
But my mother never was tested, so I didn't really have a clear understanding as what all was being done on a lot of that.

31
00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.888
Can you tell me more about the buyouts?

32
00:02:20.888 --> 00:02:21.640
The first buyouts.

33
00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:32.040
All I can remember is that they got letters from Vista and they were saying that they were going to buy . . . Offering to buy them out.

34
00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:40.840
They had in there what they were offering them as the purchase price for their homes.

35
00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:51.360
And a lot of people, from what I can understand, they had a group that went to them and said,

36
00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:56.040
"Okay if you sign this paper you're going to get this amount of money."

37
00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:03.680
And they didn't really have a good understanding as to what a share was.

38
00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:12.880
Because I think, if I'm not mistaken, they were paid by the share and the people that had gotten them to sign up,

39
00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:22.000
when they did find out what amount they were getting, some were really disappointed because it was nowhere near what they thought they were getting.

40
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:27.940
I remember telling my mother not to sign if she wasn't comfortable with doing it,

41
00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:34.300
and she was really concerned that if she signed that might have some kind of effect on my job.

42
00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:39.380
And I said, "Honey, if they're going to let me go they're going to let me go whether you sign or not."

43
00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:44.020
I said, "Just . . . I just don't want you to be left by yourself back here.

44
00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.900
Everybody else is selling and moving out."

45
00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:51.500
Because it was going to be really deserted.

46
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.160
So she kind of waited.

47
00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:56.240
She didn't sign up when she got the first letter.

48
00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:05.540
And I went with . . . My sister had come from Houston and she and I went to meetings so we could try to hear some of what they were saying.

49
00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:16.200
Judge Gray was there and he was telling the people to sign up and they could not . . . Sasol did not have . . . I think he called it Sasol,

50
00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:25.040
maybe it was Condea Vista, didn't have the right to force them, I think is what he said, for them to sign.

51
00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:34.860
So people then started I think getting a little more comfortable about receiving the letters and not feeling that this is something that they really,

52
00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.100
really had to do.

53
00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:43.700
My mother did eventually sign to move, but she was at the very last couple of days.

54
00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:48.300
She barely got in before they shut down the buyout date.

55
00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.200
And what happened to the home?

56
00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.220
Your childhood home.

57
00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:53.260
They gave them an option.

58
00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:57.180
You could sell the house yourself.

59
00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:00.180
They would buy it, but then you could take the house and sell it,

60
00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:04.540
but you had to have it off the property by the time they gave you the money.

61
00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:11.720
So if you . . . The day you got your money, your check for your house and property, you had to be off the property.

62
00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:14.060
You couldn't go back.

63
00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:22.480
So, you know, some people were able to sell their homes and get a little extra money, and then others were not.

64
00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:29.000
So if you didn't sell to someone else, then they just went in and had somebody to tear it down.

65
00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:36.700
So you had to try to get out everything that you needed and wanted out of there before you accepted that check.

66
00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:42.940
Now they did pay additional monies for I think they called it water contamination.

67
00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:46.820
I'm not too sure, but I think they did pay that.

68
00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:50.560
So that was additional monies that they got.

69
00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:52.980
And that was . . . Who got that money?

70
00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:54.500
The residents.

71
00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:58.920
And, like, if you had lived . . . had been a resident of the community,

72
00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:02.480
but you had to have proof that you had lived there.

73
00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:08.260
You had to have documentation for the number of years that you were claiming that you lived there.

74
00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:18.520
So they gave you a list of things that you could have for your documentation as having lived there for the number of years that you said.

75
00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.580
And you'd have to bring that with you when you would go to a meeting.
